=You are building a content brief for a B2B blog post targeting the keyword: {{ $json.keyword }}

Below are the top 3 pages currently ranking for this keyword. Read them and extract what the post needs to cover to compete.

{{ $json.pages.map((p, i) => `COMPETITOR ${i + 1}: ${p.title}\nURL: ${p.url}\n${p.body_text}`).join('\n\n---\n\n') }}

Return only JSON in this exact shape:
{
  "shared_subtopics": ["topic every competitor covers, so the post must include it"],
  "content_gaps": ["something none of the competitors cover well, a real opportunity"],
  "recommended_headings": ["a suggested H2/H3 heading for the post, in order"],
  "format_note": "one sentence on whether competitors are blog posts, product pages, or something else, and what that means for whether this keyword suits a blog post"
}

=Write a B2B blog post for an AI automation agency, targeting the keyword: {{ $('GroupByKeyword').item.json.keyword }}

Use this structure, based on competitor research:
Recommended headings: {{ $json.output[0].content[0].text.recommended_headings.join(', ') }}

Cover these subtopics, since competitors all include them and skipping them would hurt rankings:
{{ $json.output[0].content[0].text.shared_subtopics.join(', ') }}

Address these gaps, since none of the top-ranking competitors cover them well, this is where the post can stand out:
{{ $json.output[0].content[0].text.content_gaps.join(', ') }}

Write 1200 to 1800 words in markdown, with H2 and H3 headings matching the recommended structure. Voice: confident, direct, practical B2B tone, no filler, no hedging language, written for a business owner or operations leader evaluating AI automation, not a developer. Avoid generic AI-written phrasing like "In today's fast-paced world" or "it's important to note." End with a short, non-pushy call to action inviting the reader to explore AI automation for their business.

Return only the markdown blog post, no commentary before or after it.

